-- A call passes a binder upward without the caller having to see it.
--
-- PROPS-REDTEAM-2026-09-03.md §2.2, "Across sections": `f` reads `alpha` from
-- its own section and inherits `beta` through `g`, which is declared in a
-- section `f` does not sit under. The read-set is the union, so the directive
-- supplies both.

§ `1`
    GIVEN alpha IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
f MEANS alpha PLUS g

§ `2`
    GIVEN beta IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
g MEANS beta TIMES 2

#EVAL f WITH alpha IS 1, beta IS 2
#EVAL g WITH beta IS 10

-- Overriding only `beta` at the call to `g`: `alpha` keeps flowing to `f`.
§ `3`

GIVETH A NUMBER
h MEANS alpha PLUS (g WITH beta IS 100)

#EVAL h WITH alpha IS 1
